s it  was under the influence of the greater  will  looking at him in this way ratagan's end  of becoming a tool of the greater will  in another way this time as a sword for  its beast is thematically fitting in  life and in death ratagon is a tool of  this outer god being sent on each and  every mission it had for him he seems to  have been able to find some loved ones  along the way but his life's overriding  purpose was always that as an arm of the  order a purpose that stretched even  beyond his final breaths he becomes the  sword that is the elden beast's weapon  in the last fight of eldon ring however  the elden beast boss fight is utter  trash and that unfortunately makes me  feel sad to have a grand character and  final boss fight like ratagon being  co-opted by the lesser amorphous blob  run around for 10 minutes boss fight i  don't have any more of a thematic way to  end this video so i will conclude by  saying that radagon is cool even with  his religious zealotry and that i'm not  actually done with the video i have a  couple more points about ratagon that i  couldn't fit into the script naturally  so i'm just going to bring them up now  first is a note about something we can  find in ferum azula what looks like a  design of an old elden ring maybe what  it looked like during the age of the  dragons of note is the lack of ratagan's  rune however the tree roots overlapping  the ring look like they could be an old  version of the rune with similar but  more natural criss-crossing maybe  radigan's rune came into being when he  fused with america and the elden ring  took on a new design  another thing is that the sealed gates  in rio lucaria seem to have a design  similar to radagon's rune  that's about all i have on that one they  just look similar  and lastly is a note about viewing  ratagon and america as the revies others  like xeostorm and people on the elden  ring subreddit have identified quite a  number of alchemical references in eldon  rings world 